[2020-09-17T21:52:36Z] user_00012: I am perfectly comfortable with us inventing a `PacketBufferHandle` class that has the minimal set of semantics that we want, if people are ok with us doing our own thing.

I think we want:

1. Construction from a `PacketBuffer*` addrefs the `PacketBuffer`.
1. Construction from a `PacketBufferHandle&&` steals the value.
1. Default-construction is allowed.
1. All other constructors (specifically the copy ctor) are deleted.
1. Construction from `PacketBuffer*` is protected; handles are vended by either `PacketBuffer` factory methods or by cloning an existing handle.
1. Assignment operators other than one taking `PacketBufferHandler&&` are deleted.
1. Destruction frees the `PacketBuffer`.

I think that more or less satisfies our use case, right?

