 #### Problem
IDF build system generates sdkconfig.h from sdkconfig (built via `make menuconfig`)
GN-built files rely on the values in here (e.g. Platform initializes default SSID/PWD based on this file)
GN does not add a dependency on sdkconfig.h (-MMD option is passed when computing dependencies)

Generally the sdkconfig is a sideeffect include from:

```
In file included from /opt/espressif/esp-idf/components/newlib/platform_include/assert.h:20,
                 from /opt/espressif/esp-idf/components/esp_common/include/esp_err.h:18,
                 from /workspaces/connectedhomeip/examples/wifi-echo/server/esp32/third_party/connectedhomeip/src/platform/ESP32/CHIPPlatformConfig.h:28,
                 from /workspaces/connectedhomeip/examples/wifi-echo/server/esp32/third_party/connectedhomeip/src/system/SystemConfig.h:70,
                 from /workspaces/connectedhomeip/examples/wifi-echo/server/esp32/third_party/connectedhomeip/src/ble/BleConfig.h:42,
                 from /workspaces/connectedhomeip/examples/wifi-echo/server/esp32/third_party/connectedhomeip/src/lib/core/CHIPConfig.h:42,
                 from /workspaces/connectedhomeip/examples/wifi-echo/server/esp32/third_party/connectedhomeip/src/include/platform/CHIPDeviceConfig.h:31,
                 from /workspaces/connectedhomeip/examples/wifi-echo/server/esp32/third_party/connectedhomeip/src/include/platform/CHIPDeviceLayer.h:21,
                 from /workspaces/connectedhomeip/examples/wifi-echo/server/esp32/third_party/connectedhomeip/src/include/platform/internal/CHIPDeviceLayerInternal.h:22,
                 from ../../../../../../config/esp32/third_party/connectedhomeip/src/platform/ESP32/ConnectivityManagerImpl.cpp:22:
/workspaces/connectedhomeip/examples/wifi-echo/server/esp32/build/include/sdkconfig.h
```

Current understanding is that skdconfig.h is assumed to be a system include so it is not added as a dependency. When skdconfig is changed (`make menuconfig`) that will regenerate the header however libCHIP with gn is not rebuilt. This makes only clean builds work if sdkconfig is changed.

 #### Proposed Solution
Unsure ... building everything with GN may be ideal, but apart from that, any improvement would be good.

 #### Problem
By the nature of Messaging Layer, we need a basic protocol to sanity test the connectivity of the Messaging Layer on a higher level. In OpenWeave, this protocol is Echo. We will have echo feature implemented in cluster, but we also need a Echo protocol on protocol layer for basic connectivity test.

 #### Proposed Solution
Implement Echo protocol along side with Echo cluster for connectivity test for Messaging Layer. Then port existing test scripts from OpenWeave Happy/Cirque to CHIP for end to end test using this protocol.

@user_00003 @user_00011 @user_00004 

@user_00001 please lets me know if you are ok with this plan or not.

https://github.com/project-chip/connectedhomeip/blob/master/src/platform/ESP32/nimble/BLEManagerImpl.cpp#L408-L411

This continues delaying even after "NimBLE host task" is up and running and adds up to quite a lot of delay over time.

@user_00067

