body:
 #### Problem

Instructions for Thread demo setup  for nRF52840 DK in https://github.com/project-chip/connectedhomeip/blob/master/docs/guides/nrfconnect_android_commissioning.md use a particular `radvd` config:

```
interface wlo1
{
  MinRtrAdvInterval 3;
  MaxRtrAdvInterval 4;
  AdvSendAdvert on;
  AdvManagedFlag on;
  prefix 2001:db8:2::/64
  {
     AdvValidLifetime 14300;
     AdvPreferredLifetime 14200;
  };
};
```

The advertised prefix is of global scope, for an arbitrary GUA prefix which would not be properly routable. This causes the connecting Android phone to detect invalid IPv6 configuration in some situations (due to lack of routability), which may cause odd demo/development behaviors and also cause networking issues with the Android phone involved.

This was seen by @user_00071 during development.

 #### Proposed Solution

Suggest changing the prefix of all `radvd.conf` in demos to `fd11:db8:2::/64` or another other *random* _ULA_ prefix, which would not be clashing with anything else in a mobile Device's network config.

`<iterator>` includes `<iostream>` which leads me to believe we need to ban this header (we don't want to use huge standard library features like iostream in constrained code).

Furthermore, it's breaking the K32W build by bringing in locale support (arguably the problem is in K32W SDK, but we absolutely do not want to bring in localization support).

