 #### Problem
Looking at CASESession.cpp we do things like: 
```
    VerifyOrExit(msg_R2_Signed.Alloc(msg_r2_signed_len), err = CHIP_ERROR_NO_MEMORY);

    err = ConstructTBS2Data(responderOpCert, responderOpCertLen, msg_R2_Signed.Get(), msg_r2_signed_len);
...
    err = remoteCredential.ECDSA_validate_msg_signature(msg_R2_Signed.Get(), msg_r2_signed_len, sigmaR2SignedData);

```
which allocates some nontrivially sized buffer, fills it with things, then checks the signature.

Similarly, on the other side, we do:
```
    VerifyOrExit(msg_R2_Signed.Alloc(msg_r2_signed_len), err = CHIP_ERROR_NO_MEMORY);
....
    err = mOpCredSet->SignMsg(mTrustedRootId, msg_R2_Signed.Get(), msg_r2_signed_len, sigmaR2Signature);
```

which requires us to allocate 

 #### Proposed Solution
Use `ECDSA_validate_hash_signature` instead of `ECDSA_validate_msg_signature`, and just build up the hash to validate as we go instead of building up the entire TBS.  I suspect the hash buffer can be smaller than the TBS buffer....

Similarly, we can use `ECDSA_sign_hash` instead of `ECDSA_sign_msg` (which is what `SignMsg` above calls) to avoid having to build up the TBS in memory on the signing side....

