body:
 #### Problem

During commissioning, commissionees are inferring nodeId (for accessories themselves) from destination nodeId of incoming packets, as in `src/transport/SecureSessionMgr.cpp`
```cpp
// TODO: Remove temporary code once AddOptCert is implemented
if (packetHeader.GetDestinationNodeId().HasValue())
{
    localNodeId = packetHeader.GetDestinationNodeId().Value();
    if (localNodeId != kUndefinedNodeId && fabric->GetNodeId() != localNodeId)
    {
        fabric->SetNodeId(localNodeId);
        ChipLogProgress(Inet, "Setting nodeID %" PRIX64 " on fabric.", fabric->GetNodeId());
        modifiedFabric = true;
    }
}
```

This causes inconsistency especially with the fact that [some part of SDK](https://github.com/project-chip/connectedhomeip/blob/81a9fe6a71ee58cd5d29a6d038833746f2a68d51/src/protocols/secure_channel/CASESession.cpp#L1058) is now deriving the nodeIds from certificates (the right way): `nodeOperationalCertificate.mSubjectDN.GetCertChipId(nodeId)`

This doesn't break the in-tree examples since the destination nodeId is set by commissioner and is same as the one (unreasonably) expected to be incorporated in certificates during NOC request, even with the new API [`setNodeIdForNextNextNOCRequest(nodeId)` then `generateNOCChain(csr, ...)` has the same behavior in that sense as `generateNOCChain(nodeId, csr, ...)`].

This issue is also intented to highlight [the previous comment at a related issue](https://github.com/project-chip/connectedhomeip/issues/8227#issuecomment-887096419).

With the [recent changes](https://github.com/project-chip/connectedhomeip/pull/8137) and inconsistencies in nodeId for devices, this issue causes inconsistent DestinationIDs (for SigmaR1) and breaks CASE establishment for infrastructures that generate unique nodeIds during NOC allocation (instead of incorporating nodeIds provided by the commissioner into NOC).

Also, fabricId is not retrieved from certificates either and devices use a hard-coded value (or a test identity when flag `DEVICE_CONFIG_ENABLE_TEST_DEVICE_IDENTITY` is set) from configuration manager.

 #### Proposed Solution

Derive identities from certificates once provisioned, and use the same for advertising the device.

