[2021-09-23T04:15:12Z] user_00012: @user_00058 Sorry for the lag.  We _could_ push the session expiration further down into the networking stack so it doesn't actually get expired until after we have done the message send.  It's all doable; it would just need to change the API contracts all up the callstack to until we get out of the exchange message handling....

@user_00018 We want to clean up the session ASAP, not async, so no more messages will come in on it after fabric deletion.  Or at least that's my impression based on why #9571 happened.  As in, once we have removed the fabric, things on that fabric should not be able to change the node's state anymore.

