body:
 #### Problem
    char * tokens  = strdup(type);
    char * regtype = strtok(tokens, ".");
    free(tokens);

Current code has ^. strtok doesn't create a copy of tokens - it just creates a pointer. Free should happen at the end. But actually we should really be using a null checked safe string copy (MemoryAllocString / MemoryFree) and checking for null. Also strtok is not reentrant.

 #### Proposed Solution
option 1) Given that this platform impl already uses vector, why not use a c++ string?
option 2) strtok -> strtok_r, use MemoryAllocString, add check that tokens != null, move free to end.

