[2021-12-20T18:33:54Z] user_00012: Looking at the places that null out `mExchangeCtxt` in `CASESession`:
* `CASESession::OnResponseTimeout`: explicitly documents that we are nulling it out because the exchange will be closing itself, so we want to avoid a double-close.
* `CASESession::HandleSigma2Resume`: Does not send a response or claim it will, so the exchange will close itself as soon as this function returns.  We could _probably_ not null things out here as long as we ensured that we null the exchange pointer out in `OnExchangeClosing` (which we would need to implement).
* `CASESession::HandleSigma3`: Same thing as Sigma2Resume.
* `CASESession::OnSuccessStatusReport`: Same thing as Sigma2Resume.
* `CASESession::OnMessageReceived`: explicitly documents that we are nulling it out because the exchange will be closing itself, so we want to avoid a double-close.

Similar for `PASESession`:
* `PASESession::OnResponseTimeout`: explicitly documents that we are nulling it out because the exchange will be closing itself, so we want to avoid a double-close.
* `PASESession::HandleMsg3`: Does not send a response or claim it will, so the exchange will close itself as soon as this function returns.  We could _probably_ not null things out here as long as we ensured that we null the exchange pointer out in `OnExchangeClosing` (which we would need to implement).
* `PASESession::OnSuccessStatusReport`: Same thing as HandleMsg3.
* `PASESession::OnMessageReceived`: explicitly documents that we are nulling it out because the exchange will be closing itself, so we want to avoid a double-close.

