[2021-12-23T19:57:01Z] user_00058: Apparently this is known:

```
void OperationalDeviceProxy::DeferCloseCASESession()
{
    // Defer the release for the pending Ack to be sent
    mSystemLayer->ScheduleWork(CloseCASESessionTask, this);
}
```

The above does work.

My personal critique is that it would be very useful if success callbacks could actually indicate that the stack is done with an object.  For this problem (and #13237), this would imply sending ACK and closing the exchange _before_ calling back.  That would be far easier to deal with.  This all looks really fragile.

