 #### Problem

When using the `EstablishPASEConnection` API in `CHIPDeviceController` followed by the `Commission` API, commissioning gets stuck, since the `CommissioneeDeviceProxy` never transitions to the connected state. Since the PASE session was successfully established, commissioning should move forward. The hang is encountered in `CHIPDeviceController.cpp`:

```
if (device->IsSecureConnected())
{
    mAutoCommissioner.StartCommissioning(device);
}
else
{
    mRunCommissioningAfterConnection = true;
}
```

As it reaches the else case waiting for a subsequent connection, which never comes (as the connection has already completed).

