body:
 #### Problem
The Linux wifi driver has code like so:
```
932 memcpy(ssidStr, ssid.data(), ssid.size());
933 memcpy(keyStr, credentials.data(), credentials.size());
934 g_variant_builder_add(&builder, "{sv}", "ssid", g_variant_new_string(ssidStr));
935 g_variant_builder_add(&builder, "{sv}", "psk", g_variant_new_string(keyStr));
```
in src/platform/Linux/ConnectivityManagerImpl.cpp 

If someone passes an SSID of length `kMaxWiFiSSIDLength` this is going to read past end of buffer when calling `g_variant_new_string`...  Similar for the key string.

 #### Proposed Solution
Either use an API that can accept non-null-terminated strings, or ensure that `ssidStr` and `keyStr` have an extra byte at the end and are always null-terminated.

@user_00014 when you add vector support for multiple attribute in chip-tool,  could you help extend vector support for the below optional DataVersion, DataVersion filter is per path.

@user_00018 @user_00012

_Originally posted by @user_00030 in https://github.com/project-chip/connectedhomeip/pull/15787#r819895959_

 #### Problem
I have enabled `MfgSpecificPing` command in `Basic` cluster in ZAP tool. And regenerated code using `run_zaptool.sh`.

This is the generated code:
 
```C
void DispatchServerCommand(CommandHandler *apCommandObj,
                           const ConcreteCommandPath &aCommandPath,
                           TLV::TLVReader &aDataTlv) {
  CHIP_ERROR TLVError = CHIP_NO_ERROR;
  bool wasHandled = false;
  {
    switch (aCommandPath.mCommandId) {
    case Commands::MfgSpecificPing::Id: {
      Commands::MfgSpecificPing::DecodableType commandData;
      TLVError = DataModel::Decode(aDataTlv, commandData);
      if (TLVError == CHIP_NO_ERROR) {
        wasHandled = emberAfBasicClusterMfgSpecificPingCallback(
            apCommandObj, aCommandPath, commandData);
      }
      break;
    }
    default: {
      // Unrecognized command ID, error status will apply.
...
  }
}
```
As you can see, the line:
```C
        wasHandled = emberAfBasicClusterMfgSpecificPingCallback(
            apCommandObj, aCommandPath, commandData);
```
calls `emberAfBasicClusterMfgSpecificPingCallback` with 3 parameters. But, currently, all examples just define the function with only one parameter. It makes the project unable to be built.

https://github.com/project-chip/connectedhomeip/blob/b5a0754e008bcaf3e191ff3390b61e5f3c330604/examples/all-clusters-app/esp32/main/DeviceCallbacks.cpp#L287


 * expected behavior:
`emberAfBasicClusterMfgSpecificPingCallback` has 3 parameters.

 * actual behavior
All `emberAfBasicClusterMfgSpecificPingCallback` in all examples have only one parameters.

 * steps to reproduce
Enable `MfgSpecificPing` in zap.
 * system configuration
    * ESP32
    * using connectedhomeip tag: TE8-rc3
 * screenshots, images, logs, etc.


 #### Proposed Solution
<suggested fix, suggested enhancement>

