body:
Finding ID NCC-E003350-EXE

 #### Problem
Never repeating a NONCE is critical to AES-CCM security, and the specification states that when a message counter for a secure session saturates, that session / session key is to be invalidated.

Yet [`LocalSessionMessageCounter::Advance`](https://github.com/project-chip/connectedhomeip/blob/4967c0e0a51e3e0f0216c551d35b4cbde5aea7e4/src/transport/MessageCounter.h#L92) has no checks that the message counter of a node rolled over after it has been incremented.

For reference, `4.5.5. Counter Processing of Outgoing Messages` of the specification mandates:

> - If the message counter wraps around from 0xFFFF_FFFF to 0x0000_0000 and the message is of [Secure Unicast Session Type](https://github.com/project-chip/connectedhomeip/issues/new#ref_Session_Type):
> 
>   - The Encryption Key SHALL be expired in the [Session Context](https://github.com/project-chip/connectedhomeip/issues/new#ref_SecureSessionContext). The session will need to be renegotiated to resume communication after transmission of this final message.
> 

 #### Proposed Solution

Ensure that the counter never wraps up from its initial random value, at which point the
existing message security key must be discarded and a new key must be agreed by the
communicating peers.

Location
Function SessionManager::PrepareMessage()  in file SessionManager.cpp:L130
```
++mValue;
return CHIP_NO_ERROR;
}
private:
uint32_t mValue;
};
```

