body:
 #### Problem

Observed on these platforms: ESP32, Ameba, FreeRTOS, mbed

In init:

```
CHIP_ERROR InitClock_RealTime()
{
    Clock::Microseconds64 curTime =
        Clock::Microseconds64((static_cast<uint64_t>(CHIP_SYSTEM_CONFIG_VALID_REAL_TIME_THRESHOLD) * UINT64_C(1000000)));
    // Use CHIP_SYSTEM_CONFIG_VALID_REAL_TIME_THRESHOLD as the initial value of RealTime.
    // Then the RealTime obtained from GetClock_RealTime will be always valid.
    return System::SystemClock().SetClock_RealTime(curTime);
}
```

This is not the right thing to do.  This makes the platform believe and report that it does have wall clock time, even defeating its own rudimentary check in the getter:

```
CHIP_ERROR ClockImpl::GetClock_RealTime(Microseconds64 & aCurTime)
{
    struct timeval tv;
    if (gettimeofday(&tv, nullptr) != 0)
    {   
        return CHIP_ERROR_POSIX(errno);
    }
    if (tv.tv_sec < CHIP_SYSTEM_CONFIG_VALID_REAL_TIME_THRESHOLD)
    {   
        return CHIP_ERROR_REAL_TIME_NOT_SYNCED;
    }
    if (tv.tv_usec < 0)
    {   
        return CHIP_ERROR_REAL_TIME_NOT_SYNCED;
    }
    static_assert(CHIP_SYSTEM_CONFIG_VALID_REAL_TIME_THRESHOLD >= 0, "We might be letting through negative tv_sec values!");
    aCurTime = Microseconds64((static_cast<uint64_t>(tv.tv_sec) * UINT64_C(1000000)) + static_cast<uint64_t>(tv.tv_usec));
    return CHIP_NO_ERROR;
}
```

Because the clock is initialized to CHIP_SYSTEM_CONFIG_VALID_REAL_TIME_THRESHOLD (the chip epoch), the system will never discover that it does not have wall clock time and can never properly bubble up the CHIP_ERROR_REAL_TIME_NOT_SYNCED error.

 #### Proposed Solution

At a bare minimum, the platform would need to always return CHIP_ERROR_UNSUPPORTED_CHIP_FEATURE from its GetClock_RealTime methods to be spec compliant.

Better would be to set a flag that can capture whether the clock really has been set.

 #### Problem
I'm reading global attributes outside the context of any cluster.  To read the attributes, I need the type traits of the attribute value, but that information is only available within the context of clusters.

For example, I'm trying to read the AttributeList from all clusters using its global ID.  All clusters have it, so I don't need to care which cluster I'm looking at:

```
namespace chip {
namespace app {
namespace Clusters {
namespace Globals {  // <-- Globals namespace
namespace Attributes {
namespace AttributeList {
static constexpr AttributeId Id = 0x0000FFFB;  // <-- Attribute ID of AttributeList for all clusters
} // namespace AttributeList
```

I would expect to find its TypeInfo struct in [cluster-objects.h](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/project-chip/connectedhomeip/master/zzz_generated/app-common/app-common/zap-generated/cluster-objects.h), but this code does not exist:

```
namespace chip {
namespace app {
namespace Clusters {
namespace Globals {   // <-- Globals namespace
namespace Attributes {
namespace AttributeList {
struct TypeInfo
{
    using Type             = chip::app::DataModel::List<const chip::AttributeId>;
    using DecodableType    = chip::app::DataModel::DecodableList<chip::AttributeId>;
    using DecodableArgType = const chip::app::DataModel::DecodableList<chip::AttributeId> &;

...
```

However, it is repeated for every cluster.  E.g.:

```
namespace chip {
namespace app {
namespace Clusters {
namespace Descriptor {  // <-- Cluster namespace
namespace Attributes {
namespace AttributeList {
struct TypeInfo
{
    using Type             = chip::app::DataModel::List<const chip::AttributeId>;
    using DecodableType    = chip::app::DataModel::DecodableList<chip::AttributeId>;
    using DecodableArgType = const chip::app::DataModel::DecodableList<chip::AttributeId> &;

...
```

I'd rather not use the type traits of an arbitrary cluster.  I'd like the type traits available within the global context.

 #### Proposed Solution
Make `struct TypeInfo` available for global attributes within the `chip::app::Clusters::Globals::Attributes` namespace.

