 #### Problem

Discovered when running a wildcard read on all attributes via `chip-tool any read-by-id 0xffffffff 0xffffffff 1 0xffff`.

If the ACL cluster tries to encode its attributes and cannot complete, due to the buffer space being exhausted, it will translate its internal error code `CHIP_ERROR_NO_MEMORY` into `CHIP_IM_GLOBAL_STATUS(ResourceExhausted)`. This is done in `ChipErrorToImErrorMap()`.

The report engine, namely the function `Engine::BuildSingleReportDataAttributeReportIBs()` will only test for CHIP_ERROR_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL and CHIP_ERROR_NO_MEMORY to enable chunking.

```c++
    if ((err == CHIP_ERROR_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL) || (err == CHIP_ERROR_NO_MEMORY))
    {
        ChipLogDetail(DataManagement, "<RE:Run> We cannot put more chunks into this report. Enable chunking.");

        //
        // Reset the error tracked within the builder. Otherwise, any further attempts to write
        // data through the builder will be blocked by that error.
        //
        attributeReportIBs.ResetError();
        err = CHIP_NO_ERROR;
    }
```
If an `CHIP_IM_GLOBAL_STATUS(ResourceExhausted)` is encountered, processing will fail and the error code will be propagated back over the wire to the requestor.

DUT log:
```
2022-08-30 12:55:38.139176 I DMG          Re-mapped src/system/TLVPacketBufferBackingStore.cpp:88: CHIP Error 0x0000000B: No memory into src/system/TLVPacketBufferBackingStore.cpp:88: CHIP Error 0x0000000B: No memory for IM return codes
2022-08-30 12:55:38.139204 I DMG          Error retrieving data from clusterId: 0x0000_001F, err = src/app/clusters/access-control-server/access-control-server.cpp:450: IM Error 0x00000589: General error: 0x89 (RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED)
2022-08-30 12:55:38.139236 I DMG          <RE:Run> Cluster 1f, Attribute fffc is dirty
```

chip-tool output:
```
# chip-tool any read-by-id 0xffffffff 0xffffffff 1 0xffff
...
[1661856926.330258][39297:39298] CHIP:DMG:              AttributeReportIB =
[1661856926.330264][39297:39298] CHIP:DMG:              {
[1661856926.330268][39297:39298] CHIP:DMG:                      AttributeStatusIB =
[1661856926.330273][39297:39298] CHIP:DMG:                      {
[1661856926.330278][39297:39298] CHIP:DMG:                              AttributePathIB =
[1661856926.330353][39297:39298] CHIP:DMG:                              {
[1661856926.330359][39297:39298] CHIP:DMG:                                      Endpoint = 0x0,
[1661856926.330367][39297:39298] CHIP:DMG:                                      Cluster = 0x1f,
[1661856926.330372][39297:39298] CHIP:DMG:                                      Attribute = 0x0000_0004,
[1661856926.330412][39297:39298] CHIP:DMG:                              }
[1661856926.330422][39297:39298] CHIP:DMG: 
[1661856926.330427][39297:39298] CHIP:DMG:                              StatusIB =
[1661856926.330468][39297:39298] CHIP:DMG:                              {
[1661856926.330475][39297:39298] CHIP:DMG:                                      status = 0x89 (RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED),
[1661856926.330480][39297:39298] CHIP:DMG:                              },
[1661856926.330518][39297:39298] CHIP:DMG: 
[1661856926.330524][39297:39298] CHIP:DMG:                      },
[1661856926.330530][39297:39298] CHIP:DMG: 
[1661856926.330534][39297:39298] CHIP:DMG:              },
[1661856926.330575][39297:39298] CHIP:DMG: 
...
[1661856938.197042][39301:39301] CHIP:TOO: Run command failure: IM Error 0x00000589: General error: 0x89 (RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED)
```

So far, we could unfortunately only reproduce this situation with our DUT, not with any of the example applications.

 #### Proposed Solution
Either have `Engine::BuildSingleReportDataAttributeReportIBs()` test for `CHIP_IM_GLOBAL_STATUS(ResourceExhausted)` or have the ACL cluster return `CHIP_ERROR_NO_MEMORY` or `CHIP_ERROR_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL`.

We fixed this with the following patch:

```diff
diff --git a/src/app/reporting/Engine.cpp b/src/app/reporting/Engine.cpp
index 792631f..b2f18da 100644
--- a/src/app/reporting/Engine.cpp
+++ b/src/app/reporting/Engine.cpp
@@ -189,7 +189,8 @@ CHIP_ERROR Engine::BuildSingleReportDataAttributeReportIBs(ReportDataMessage::Bu
                 // Otherwise, if partial data allowed, save the encode state.
                 // Otherwise roll back. If we have already encoded some chunks, we are done; otherwise encode status.

-                if (encodeState.AllowPartialData() && ((err == CHIP_ERROR_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL) || (err == CHIP_ERROR_NO_MEMORY)))
+                if (encodeState.AllowPartialData() && ((err == CHIP_ERROR_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL) || (err == CHIP_ERROR_NO_MEMORY) ||
+                        (err == CHIP_IM_GLOBAL_STATUS(ResourceExhausted))))
                 {
                     // Encoding is aborted but partial data is allowed, then we don't rollback and save the state for next chunk.
                     apReadHandler->SetAttributeEncodeState(encodeState);
@@ -201,7 +202,8 @@ CHIP_ERROR Engine::BuildSingleReportDataAttributeReportIBs(ReportDataMessage::Bu
                     attributeReportIBs.Rollback(attributeBackup);
                     apReadHandler->SetAttributeEncodeState(AttributeValueEncoder::AttributeEncodeState());

-                    if (err != CHIP_ERROR_NO_MEMORY && err != CHIP_ERROR_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL)
+                    if (err != CHIP_ERROR_NO_MEMORY && err != CHIP_ERROR_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL &&
+                        err != CHIP_IM_GLOBAL_STATUS(ResourceExhausted))
                     {
                         // Try to encode our error as a status response.
                         err = attributeReportIBs.EncodeAttributeStatus(pathForRetrieval, StatusIB(err));
@@ -241,7 +243,8 @@ exit:
     // These are are guaranteed to not fail since we've already reserved memory for the remaining 'close out' TLV operations in this
     // function and its callers.
     //
-    if ((err == CHIP_ERROR_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL) || (err == CHIP_ERROR_NO_MEMORY))
+    if ((err == CHIP_ERROR_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL) || (err == CHIP_ERROR_NO_MEMORY) ||
+            (err == CHIP_IM_GLOBAL_STATUS(ResourceExhausted)))
     {
         ChipLogDetail(DataManagement, "<RE:Run> We cannot put more chunks into this report. Enable chunking.");
```

 #### Problem
 
 We need to release the buffer in case of failure.

```
void UDPEndPointImplLwIP::LwIPReceiveUDPMessage(void * arg, struct udp_pcb * pcb, struct pbuf * p, const ip_addr_t * addr,
                                                u16_t port)
{


    CHIP_ERROR err = ep->GetSystemLayer().ScheduleLambda(
        [ep, p = System::LwIPPacketBufferView::UnsafeGetLwIPpbuf(buf), pktInfo = pktInfo.get()] {
            ep->HandleDataReceived(System::PacketBufferHandle::Adopt(p), pktInfo);
        });

    if (err == CHIP_NO_ERROR)
    {
        // If ScheduleLambda() succeeded, it has ownership of the buffer, so we need to release it (without freeing it).
        static_cast<void>(std::move(buf).UnsafeRelease());
        // Similarly, ScheduleLambda now has ownership of pktInfo.
        pktInfo.release();
    }
}
```

 #### Proposed Solution
<suggested fix, suggested enhancement>

 #### Problem
According to the spec:

> [11.21.6.5. BlockEOF Message]
> The BlockEOF message represents the final block in a data transfer.
> 
> Note that, unlike a Block, BlockEOF MAY have a data length of zero. If the entire transfer fits within the negotiated block size, the BlockEOF SHALL be the one and only message sent in the exchange and no Block messages will be sent. In that trivial case, the Block Counter would be 0 in the BlockEOF.

Linux implementation currently doesn't allow this:
 
[src/platform/Linux/OTAImageProcessorImpl.cpp, line 71](https://github.com/project-chip/connectedhomeip/blob/master/src/platform/Linux/OTAImageProcessorImpl.cpp#L71)
```
    if ((block.data() == nullptr) || block.empty())
    {
        return CHIP_ERROR_INVALID_ARGUMENT;
    }
```

 #### Proposed Solution
Remove this check, it is checked immediately after in SetBlock: https://github.com/project-chip/connectedhomeip/blob/master/src/platform/Linux/OTAImageProcessorImpl.cpp#L244

But at this point the block is released correctly and it does not return an error: 
```
    if (!IsSpanUsable(block))
    {
        ReleaseBlock();
        return CHIP_NO_ERROR;
    }
 ```
 
 This also mimics how other  platforms are implemented.

