> 1. The exact way you are using Matter.framework for commissioning into your own fabric.  Are you using the automatic certificate issuer in the framework itself, or are you issuing your own certificates?  In the latter case, are you using the framework's MTRCertificates API to create the certificates or using some other CA?
> 2. What exact data is received by the commissionee for the Sigma1/Sigma3 messages and the AddTrustedRootCertificate and AddNOC commands?  If you are about to enable detail logging and set `enable_im_pretty_print=true` when compiling Matter for the device, that will show you the command payloads.  To log the Sigma1/Sigma3 payloads, you would need to add some logging code to CASESession.cpp.  If you want pointers on this, or just a diff that adds the relevant code, please let me know.
> 
> I would love to get to the bottom of this....

Hi @user_00012 ,

We are able to reproduce the issue everytime. The details of our implementation are as per the following:

### Fabric creation:
When a fabric is created we create a Root CA, it is self signed. We do not use any third party APIs to create root ca or sign the CSRs. all the requests to add a devices to above fabric will use above root ca to get NoC.
NOC Chain validation is also successful.
  

### Generating CSR for user operational certificate for controller initialization:
-   We create the key pair (kSecAttrKeyTypeECSECPrimeRandom)
-   We generate CSR using the following method:
```
+ (MTRCSRDERBytes _Nullable)createCertificateSigningRequest:(id<MTRKeypair>)keypair error:(NSError * __autoreleasing _Nullable * _Nullable)error;
```
-   This CSR is used to generate operational certificate which is passed in the controller initialisation method:
```
- (instancetype)initWithIPK:(NSData *)ipk operationalKeypair: (id<MTRKeypair>)operationalKeypair operationalCertificate:(MTRCertificateDERBytes)operationalCertificate intermediateCertificate:(MTRCertificateDERBytes _Nullable)intermediateCertificate rootCertificate:(MTRCertificateDERBytes)rootCertificate
```


### Fetching CSR for device NOC from Matter callback:
- We have created a class corresponding to MTROperationalCertificateIssuer protocol and we set this class as the operationalCertificateIssuer for the controller startup params.
- We get the CSR from the following method:
```
func issueOperationalCertificate(forRequest csrInfo: MTROperationalCSRInfo, attestationInfo: MTRDeviceAttestationInfo, controller: MTRDeviceController, completion: @escaping (MTROperationalCertificateChain?, Error?) -> Void)
```
- We use this CSR to get the NOC that we finally pass as MTROperationalCertificateChain param in the above method’s completion handler.

PFA esp32c3 and iOS app logs. Also do let me know if you need any other details on this.
[esp32c3_device_logs.log](https://github.com/project-chip/connectedhomeip/files/11554843/esp32c3_device_logs.log)
[iOS_app_logs.log](https://github.com/project-chip/connectedhomeip/files/11554844/iOS_app_logs.log)


