[2023-05-25T02:41:39Z] user_00012: > This CSR is used to generate operational certificate which is passed in the controller initialisation method

I'm not sure what "We do not use any third party APIs to create root ca or sign the CSRs" means.  This operational certificate generation (for both the device's NOC and the controller's NOC) is done by your CA, right?  I think the most important bit I need to understand here is whether you are asking Matter.framework to generate any certificates (via the MTRCertificates APIs) or whether you are generating them yourself somehow based on the CSRs involved.

As far as the logs go, the key part is understanding _exactly_ what certificates the esp32 device received both as part of commissioning and as part of the CASE handshake (so we can figure out whether the problem is with those certificates or with the validation code on the esp32 device), and neither one is present in the attached logs.

Again, to see the certificates received during commissioning you would want to compile the esp32 image with `enable_im_pretty_print=true` and detail logging enabled (and debug-level logging enabled for the esp32 build you are using).  To see the CASE payloads you would need to add logging to CASESession.  Perhaps something like this: 
[CASE-logging.patch](https://github.com/project-chip/connectedhomeip/files/11560633/CASE-logging.patch)


