[2023-06-02T20:58:28Z] user_00012: @user_00314 So comparing what you have above to things I know work:

1. I'm a little surprised you are storing your _public_ key in the keychain.  What I would have assumed you do is you store the private key, and then `SecKeyCopyPublicKey` to get the public key from the private key.  I have no idea whether this is a problem in practice or not.  And I think we _are_ checking that your op key pair's public key matches the opcert, so I guess I have to assume this is OK...  Especially if that's how you are getting the public key to do your CSR with.
2. I'm confused by the fact that you generate a new IPK every time.  I don't see how that can work across restarts, but I am assuming in your commissioning flow you are not restarting, so I would not have expected this to affect commissioning.

> Note: Initially we had used hardcoded CSR and key pair and that was working but that too has stopped working with the same error.

"has stopped working" after what?



