[2023-07-21T18:55:06Z] user_00012: > These productAttestationAuthorityCertificates do I need to apply for?

No, these are just the entities that you trust to tell you devices are certified.  It's your decision as to what those entities are.

The full set of known PAA certs can be gotten from the .der files in `credentials/production/paa-root-certs` in the source tree (might be somewhat out of date; it gets synced to the DCL periodically) or directly from the DCL (see https://blog.espressif.com/matter-distributed-compliance-ledger-dcl-4013c2376e7 or https://developer.nordicsemi.com/nRF_Connect_SDK/doc/2.2.0/nrf/ug_matter_device_dcl.html or https://csa-iot.org/certification/distributed-compliance-ledger/) for some explanations, but I don't see obvious step-by-step bits to programmatically download all PAAs if that's what you want.

> Currently I only want to control one device with its own fabric and device controller for testing.

Then you only need to trust PAA that certified that specific device.

> But if I understand correctly, this is only possible with the credentials to the ThreadNetwork my iPods?
> Are there any alternatives?

I am not sure what you are asking.  If you use MatterSupport, that will give the device the Thread credentials so it can join the Thread network.  Then you can control it, after commissioning it into your own fabric.  Are you looking for a way to have it _not_ join the Thread network?


