Tracking issue for the change in type of the OperationalState attribute to cover needed SDK changes. 
See PR: https://github.com/CHIP-Specifications/chip-test-plans/issues/2963

@user_00514

### Reproduction steps

**Tested Environment: Android Device** 
- Chromecast 4K Android 12 (armeabi-v7a)
- GiGA Genie 3 (KAON KI1100) Android 11 (armeabi-v7a)

**ABI: armeabi-v7a (32bit)** 

1. Problem
I am trying to get end-device's specific value, such as deviceTypeId of matter light bulb, so i am calling code below: 
```
 @OptIn(ExperimentalCoroutinesApi::class)
    suspend fun loadDeviceType(): Long {
        val descriptorCluster = getDescriptorCluster(context, deviceId)

        return suspendCancellableCoroutine { continuation ->
            descriptorCluster.readDeviceTypeListAttribute(object: DeviceTypeListAttributeCallback{
                override fun onSuccess(valueList: MutableList<ChipStructs.DescriptorClusterDeviceTypeStruct>?) {
                    continuation.resume(valueList!![0].deviceType) {}
                }

                override fun onError(ex: Exception?) {
                    continuation.resumeWithException(ex ?: Exception("Unknown error"))
                }
            })

            continuation.invokeOnCancellation {
                Timber.tag(TAG).e("loadDeviceType cancel, $it")
            }
        }
    }
```

and returned value was : 
on arm64-v8a (Google Pixel 6, Samsung Galaxy S20 FE, Samsung Note 10, etc..)
```
269
```
on armeabi-v7a (Chromecast 4K, GiGA Genie 3 (KAON KI1100)
```
-5178014922610311676
```

**As you can see, returned deviceTypeId is different between architectures. (32bit <-> 64bit)**
Returned value from 32bit os is incorrect.

So I looked at logcat on android, and i found out that deviceTypeId value was returned correctly inside sdk. (both 32bit, 64bit)
Look at my logcat below: these are appeared logs when i called descriptorCluster.readDeviceTypeListAttribute().

```
ReportDataMessage =
{
	AttributeReportIBs =
	[
		AttributeReportIB =
		{
			AttributeDataIB =
			{
				DataVersion = 0x82102a0d,
				AttributePathIB =
				{
					Endpoint = 0x1,
					Cluster = 0x1d,
					Attribute = 0x0000_0000,
				}
					
				Data = [
						
				],
			},
			
		},
		
		AttributeReportIB =
		{
			AttributeDataIB =
			{
				DataVersion = 0x82102a0d,
				AttributePathIB =
				{
					Endpoint = 0x1,
					Cluster = 0x1d,
					Attribute = 0x0000_0000,
					ListIndex = Null,
				}
					
				Data = 
				{
					0x0 = 269, 
					0x1 = 1, 
				},
			},
			
		},
		
	],
	
	SuppressResponse = true, 
	InteractionModelRevision = 1
}
```
As far as I can predict, the value is normally obtained inside the sdk, 
but when the value is returned through JNI on 32bit android os, the wrong value appears.

This error is not just for deviceTypeId, but every (that i checked) value which type is long.

Thank you for assistance.

