@user_00093 @user_00801 

If we're going to make an API change here, we should think pretty hard about what the API should look like instead of taking EmberAfAttributeMetadata....  The type+size may not be the right thing.

Plus the various other issues.  And the fact that this breaks API compat for SDK consumers.

### Reproduction steps

The ICD Manager has to retrieve the ICD monitoring table and determine if any client is registered to become a LIT.

To do so the ICD Manager requires access to the PersistentStorageDelegate

This code block, in ICDManager.cpp, is currently commented out. Trying to use and include the PersistentStorage leads to a series of circular dependency issues between apps, servers, and data-model.

```
const auto & fabricTable = Server::GetInstance().GetFabricTable();
for (const auto & fabricInfo : fabricTable)
{
        PersistentStorageDelegate & storage = Server::GetInstance().GetPersistentStorage();
        IcdMonitoringTable table(storage, fabricInfo.GetFabricIndex(), 1);
        if (!table.IsEmpty())
        {
             tempMode = ICDMode::LIT;
             break;
         }
}
```

A solution to the dependency issue or modification to the ICDManager needs to be done to support LIT.


One potential solution would be to pass a reference to the PersistentStorageDelegate to the ICDManager init function, which is done in `server.cpp`

### Bug prevalence

Always for and ICD

