[2023-10-07T06:09:03Z] user_00012: @user_00568 Thank you, those new logs are much better from my point of view.  I see Matter things going on there!

So this log:
```
2023-10-06 09:47:06.991085+0200 0x23D6     Default   0xCFE3               505    0 MatterExtension: (MatterExtension) FAGAN: setupCommissioningSession ERROR->Error Domain=MTRErrorDomain Code=1 UserInfo={NSLocalizedDescription=<private>, errorCode=172}
```

is preceded by:
```
2023-10-06 09:47:06.983655+0200 0x23D6     Default   0xCFE3               505    0 MatterExtension: (Matter) [com.csa.matter:Controller] Starting commissioning discovery over DNS-SD
2023-10-06 09:47:06.983703+0200 0x23D6     Default   0xCFE3               505    0 MatterExtension: (Matter) [com.csa.matter:Discovery] Browsing for: _matterc._udp,_L832
...
2023-10-06 09:47:06.988258+0200 0xCAD      Error     0x0                  170    0 mDNSResponder: (mDNSResponder) [com.apple.mdns:trust] App Info.plist(NSBonjourServices) does not allow '_matterc._udp.' for (MatterExtension)
...
2023-10-06 09:47:06.988505+0200 0x23D6     Error     0xCFE3               505    0 MatterExtension: (Matter) [com.csa.matter:Default] Error(src/platform/Darwin/MdnsError.cpp:108: CHIP Error 0x000000AC: Internal error): Failure while pairing the device
```

I suspect what you want is to add
```
	<key>NSBonjourServices</key>
	<array>
		<string>_matter._tcp</string>
		<string>_matterc._udp</string>
	</array>
```
to the Info.plist for your MatterExtension.

I created https://github.com/project-chip/connectedhomeip/pull/29642 to improve the error reporting here.  With that in place, in this situation you should get an error more like this:
```
Error Domain=MTRErrorDomain Code=15  UserInfo={NSLocalizedDescription=Access denied to perform DNS-SD lookups.  Check that "_matter._tcp" and/or "_matterc._udp" are listed under the NSBonjourServices key in Info.plist}
```
(and even if that description does not appear, at least the Code=15 will let you look up what's going on in MTRError.h...)

