[2023-10-11T18:35:41Z] user_00012: @user_00727 Assuming that the error logs above correspond to the provided code:
```
Failed to read Nodelabel attribute. Status: 0xC3
```
That's UNSUPPORTED_CLUSTER.  Do you have that cluster enabled on endpoint 0?

```
 (183743) all-clusters-app: Failed to read Description attribute. Status: 0x8D 
```
That's INVALID_DATA_TYPE.  That's because you are trying to read into a 0-size buffer, so what were you expecting to happen, exactly?

The right way to read strings is more like this:
```
   char value_chars[N]; //  N needs to be at least the max size of the string data as defined in the spec
   chip::MutableCharSpan value(value_chars);
   status = ModeSelect::Attributes::Description::Get(DeviceID, value); // NOTE: Will modify `value.size()`

   // NOTE: value_chars is NOT NULL-TERMINATED, so doing things like
   //
   // ESP_LOGI(TAG, "Retrieved value: %s", value.data());
   //
   // is a great way to have security bugs.  Instead use:
   //
   // ESP_LOGI(TAG, "Retrieved value: %.*s", static_cast<int>(value.size()), value_.data());

   // Now if you want to use the same buffer for a different read, you need a new MutableCharSpan.
```

