body:
### Workflow issues

In the Yaml CI, we currently need to explicitly test for all members of complex structures even if we are only interested in certain values. For instance, in Test_TC_S_2_2 [here](https://github.com/project-chip/connectedhomeip/blob/78c8704a4e1dacacf0eef824268143c13e122e8c/src/app/tests/suites/certification/Test_TC_S_2_2.yaml#L452C1-L521C24), we are only interested in on Attibute in two clusters, but end up checking all attributes present in the struct, which is tedious and means we will need to modifiy this test each time a new extension field set is implemented in the all-cluster-app:
```
                value:
                    [
                        {
                            ClusterID: 0x0006,
                            AttributeValueList:
                                [{ AttributeID: 0x0000, AttributeValue: 0x01 }],
                        },
                        {
                            ClusterID: 0x0008,
                            AttributeValueList:
                                [{ AttributeID: 0x0000, AttributeValue: 0x64 }],
                        },
                        {
                            ClusterID: 0x0300,
                            AttributeValueList:
                                [
                                    {
                                        AttributeID: 0x0003,
                                        AttributeValue: 0x616b,
                                    },
                                    {
                                        AttributeID: 0x0004,
                                        AttributeValue: 0x607d,
                                    },
                                    {
                                        AttributeID: 0x4000,
                                        AttributeValue: 0x0000,
                                    },
                                    {
                                        AttributeID: 0x0001,
                                        AttributeValue: 0x00,
                                    },
                                    {
                                        AttributeID: 0x4002,
                                        AttributeValue: 0x00,
                                    },
                                    {
                                        AttributeID: 0x4003,
                                        AttributeValue: 0x00,
                                    },
                                    {
                                        AttributeID: 0x4004,
                                        AttributeValue: 0x0019,
                                    },
                                    {
                                        AttributeID: 0x0007,
                                        AttributeValue: 0x00,
                                    },
                                    {
                                        AttributeID: 0x4001,
                                        AttributeValue: 0x02,
                                    },
                                ],
                        },
                    ]
```

As Identified in the TODO below, we need to have a way to check only for the values that we are expecting to see a change in:
```
                #TODO : Need to change the check for a check like below if possible
                # constraints:
                #     type: list
                #     contains: [
                #         {
                #             ClusterID: 0x0006,
                #             AttributeValueList:
                #                 [{ AttributeID: 0x0000, AttributeValue: 0x01 }],
                #         },
                #         {
                #             ClusterID: 0x0008,
                #             AttributeValueList:
                #                 [{ AttributeID: 0x0000, AttributeValue: 0x64 }],
                #         },
                #     ]
```

### Platform

all

### Anything else?

_No response_

### Reproduction steps

For generating chip-tool as a OTA provider I have enabled OTA-provider cluster as a server from ZAP tool. So the process would be like below
(1) Commission OTA requestor from chip-tool
(2) Announce OTA provider(chip-tool) for presence. For this step I knew chip-tool node ID would be 112233.
(3) According to my knowledge if only chip-tool and ota requestor are involved, there would be no role of access control list(ACL) , **what should be ACL cluster in chip-tool(client/server/both)?**
Now I am facing only one error here in the function **ProcessCommandDataIB** (/src/app/CommandHandler.cpp). Here I am getting error log like this "**acl err code is src/access/AccessControl.cpp:314: CHIP Error 0x00000003: Incorrect state**"

`  {   
    ChipLogDetail(DataManagement,"cluster %x and endpoint %d\n",concretePath.mClusterId,concretePath.mEndpointId);
    Access::SubjectDescriptor subjectDescriptor = GetSubjectDescriptor();
    Access::RequestPath requestPath{ .cluster = concretePath.mClusterId, .endpoint = concretePath.mEndpointId };
    Access::Privilege requestPrivilege = RequiredPrivilege::ForInvokeCommand(concretePath);
    err                                = Access::GetAccessControl().Check(subjectDescriptor, requestPath, requestPrivilege);
    ChipLogError(DataManagement, "acl err code is %" CHIP_ERROR_FORMAT, err.Format());
    if (err != CHIP_NO_ERROR)
    {
        if (err != CHIP_ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED)
        {
           // ChipLogDetail(DataManagement,"[MS::: failed concrete path %s] \n",concretePath);
            return FallibleAddStatus(concretePath, Status::Failure) != CHIP_NO_ERROR ? Status::Failure : Status::Success;
        }
         ChipLogDetail(DataManagement,"TODO wildcard\n");
        // TODO: when wildcard invokes are supported, handle them to discard rather than fail with status
        return FallibleAddStatus(concretePath, Status::UnsupportedAccess) != CHIP_NO_ERROR ? Status::Failure : Status::Success;
    } 
}`
why this is showing incorrect state, as we are as a matter root node so it has all the privilege?

