[2024-02-16T14:03:21Z] user_00027: Well, I obviously haven't tested that so I'm not sure what else needs fixing but our unit tests use loopback endpoints to test higher layers so in theory it _should_ be possible to implement the multicast loop at lower layers than IM (networking stack in the best case, or Matter's `UDPEndpoint` as a last resort).
While this might be suboptimal in some cases (for unicast bindings you would need CASE even though the traffic doesn't go outside the device), it might simplify the protocol design as well. So it's just an idea to consider :)

