[2024-03-04T18:57:53Z] user_00012: @user_00996 These clusters ask a delegate for the values.  See https://github.com/project-chip/connectedhomeip/blob/9f6d627e0262e1d023986291948bb4e845be803e/src/app/clusters/electrical-power-measurement-server/electrical-power-measurement-server.h#L35 for example.  You implement that interface, pass your implementation to the cluster instance object you create (see https://github.com/project-chip/connectedhomeip/blob/9f6d627e0262e1d023986291948bb4e845be803e/src/app/clusters/electrical-power-measurement-server/electrical-power-measurement-server.h#L104-L110), and the functions on your interface will be called when the cluster needs an attribute value.

Note that it's your responsibility to call `MatterReportingAttributeChangeCallback` when those attribute values change.

