[2025-03-03T19:25:37Z] user_01255: For context this PR included some code that is better code-gen'd, I was tasked to provide some code on what we wanted this code to look like.

I did an investigation on all the uses of the current metadata on attributes and commands so that I could understand where and how it is used, after that I am making this proposal so I can have some feedback before committing.

I also suggest a better interface for CHIP my reasoning is the following, if we are generating the metadata in an easily consumable way, it makes no sense to copy the data unless necessary.


## Metadata Generation

Ideally it replaces current info objects so that we don't duplicate information and 
Possible con, Will need to touch a lot of functions to use this new metadata instead of the old one

So I would provide these arrays inside the Cluster Namespace either on a `Command::Entries`/`Attribute::Entries` path or directly in `Entries`, one advantage would be if we want to keep some usings so that we can read it very close to what the spec provides or if we don't care enough, I personally would not care about this but felt that it might be a thing to consider.

``` cpp

