body:
### Type

Other

### Explanation



Hello @user_00012 and @user_00256,

I'm trying to update and verify attribute values using the `ElectricalPowerMeasurementDelegate`. I used the `Set` functions to assign values and then used the corresponding `Get` functions to read them back. However, while the values appear to be set correctly in logs, they are not reflected in the CHIP REPL output.

Here is the code snippet I’m using:


```
static ElectricalPowerMeasurementDelegate gPowerDelegate;
void SimulateMeasurements()
{
    ChipLogProgress(AppServer, "Inside simulate measurement");
    int64_t voltage = 230;  // Example: 230V
    int64_t power   = 50;   // Example: 50W
    int64_t current = 10;   // Example: 10A

    // Set attributes
    gPowerDelegate.SetVoltage(DataModel::Nullable<int64_t>(voltage));
    gPowerDelegate.SetActivePower(DataModel::Nullable<int64_t>(power));
    gPowerDelegate.SetActiveCurrent(DataModel::Nullable<int64_t>(current));

    // Get attributes back and print
    auto readVoltage = gPowerDelegate.GetVoltage();
    auto readPower   = gPowerDelegate.GetActivePower();
    auto readCurrent = gPowerDelegate.GetActiveCurrent();

    if (!readVoltage.IsNull())
    {
        ChipLogProgress(AppServer, "Voltage after setting: %lld V", readVoltage.Value());
    }
    else
    {
        ChipLogError(AppServer, "Voltage is NULL after setting!");
    }

    if (!readPower.IsNull())
    {
        ChipLogProgress(AppServer, "Power after setting: %lld W", readPower.Value());
    }
    else
    {
        ChipLogError(AppServer, "Power is NULL after setting!");
    }

    if (!readCurrent.IsNull())
    {
        ChipLogProgress(AppServer, "Current after setting: %lld A", readCurrent.Value());
    }
    else
    {
        ChipLogError(AppServer, "Current is NULL after setting!");
    }
}
```

output image:
![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5abbb9e7-6263-48dd-b46b-a1d7b06a2b25)

Could you please guide me on what might be missing or if there’s an additional step required to sync these values with the actual Matter attribute storage?

Looking forward to your feedback.

Thanks!

### Platform

esp32

### Platform Version(s)

1.3

### Testing

Platform validated

### (Optional) If manually tested please explain why this is only manually tested

_No response_

### Anything else?

_No response_

It seems that there is a minor change in the StatusCode enum from AdministratorCommissioning.

The generated one based on the specs is called StatusCodeEnum instead of plainly StatusCode.

Old:
```c
// Enum for StatusCode
enum class StatusCode : uint8_t
{
    kBusy               = 0x02,
    kPAKEParameterError = 0x03,
    kWindowNotOpen      = 0x04,
    // All received enum values that are not listed above will be mapped
    // to kUnknownEnumValue. This is a helper enum value that should only
    // be used by code to process how it handles receiving and unknown
    // enum value. This specific should never be transmitted.
    kUnknownEnumValue = 0,
};
```

New:
```c
// Enum for StatusCodeEnum
enum class StatusCodeEnum : uint8_t
{
    kBusy               = 0x02,
    kPAKEParameterError = 0x03,
    kWindowNotOpen      = 0x04,
    // All received enum values that are not listed above will be mapped
    // to kUnknownEnumValue. This is a helper enum value that should only
    // be used by code to process how it handles receiving and unknown
    // enum value. This specific should never be transmitted.
    kUnknownEnumValue = 0,
};
```

It actually looks like a minor change but seems to break the compilation of some example apps so it probably also breaks compat to some extent.

There are some weird differences between the Alchemy generated (based on the spec) and the existing SDK implementation for color control.

The most meaningful one seems to be the change from `uint8_t` to `ColorLoopDirectionEnum` for the `ColorLoopDirection` attribute.

Before:
```c
namespace ColorLoopDirection {
struct TypeInfo
{
    using Type             = uint8_t;
    using DecodableType    = uint8_t;
    using DecodableArgType = uint8_t;

    static constexpr ClusterId GetClusterId() { return Clusters::ColorControl::Id; }
    static constexpr AttributeId GetAttributeId() { return Attributes::ColorLoopDirection::Id; }
    static constexpr bool MustUseTimedWrite() { return false; }
};
} // namespace ColorLoopDirection
```

After:
```c
namespace ColorLoopDirection {
struct TypeInfo
{
    using Type             = chip::app::Clusters::ColorControl::ColorLoopDirectionEnum;
    using DecodableType    = chip::app::Clusters::ColorControl::ColorLoopDirectionEnum;
    using DecodableArgType = chip::app::Clusters::ColorControl::ColorLoopDirectionEnum;

    static constexpr ClusterId GetClusterId() { return Clusters::ColorControl::Id; }
    static constexpr AttributeId GetAttributeId() { return Attributes::ColorLoopDirection::Id; }
    static constexpr bool MustUseTimedWrite() { return false; }
};
} // namespace ColorLoopDirection
```

Also the feature bitmap had a change in one of the enum elements generated from `kHueAndSaturation` to `kHueSaturation`.

Before:
```c
// Bitmap for Feature
enum class Feature : uint32_t
{
    kHueAndSaturation = 0x1,
    kEnhancedHue      = 0x2,
    kColorLoop        = 0x4,
    kXy               = 0x8,
    kColorTemperature = 0x10,
};
```

After:
```c
// Bitmap for Feature
enum class Feature : uint32_t
{
    kHueSaturation    = 0x1,
    kEnhancedHue      = 0x2,
    kColorLoop        = 0x4,
    kXy               = 0x8,
    kColorTemperature = 0x10,
};
```

The `DoorLock` cluster seems to have a couple of issues when trying to generate the code with ZAP based on the Alchemy generated XML.

1.- There is an error during the ZAP generation
```
lark.exceptions.UnexpectedToken: Unexpected token Token('ID', 'desc') at line 5803, column 3.
Expected one of: 
	* COMMAND
	* SHARED
	* PROVISIONAL
	* TIMEDWRITE
	* RBRACE
	* READONLY
	* INTERNAL
	* BITMAP
	* CRITICAL
	* DEBUG
	* ATTRIBUTE
	* INFO
	* STABLE
	* FABRIC_SCOPED
	* DEPRECATED
	* NOSUBSCRIBE
	* STRUCT
	* REQUEST
	* TIMED
	* ENUM
	* FABRIC
	* FABRIC_SENSITIVE
	* RESPONSE
Previous tokens: [Token('RBRACE', '}')]
```

2.- The `LEDSettings` attribute type changed from `uint8_t` to `LEDSettingEnum`, this may break compatibility.

Before:
```c
namespace LEDSettings {
struct TypeInfo
{
    using Type             = uint8_t;
    using DecodableType    = uint8_t;
    using DecodableArgType = uint8_t;

    static constexpr ClusterId GetClusterId() { return Clusters::DoorLock::Id; }
    static constexpr AttributeId GetAttributeId() { return Attributes::LEDSettings::Id; }
    static constexpr bool MustUseTimedWrite() { return false; }
};
} // namespace LEDSettings
```

After:
```c
namespace LEDSettings {
struct TypeInfo
{
    using Type             = chip::app::Clusters::DoorLock::LEDSettingEnum;
    using DecodableType    = chip::app::Clusters::DoorLock::LEDSettingEnum;
    using DecodableArgType = chip::app::Clusters::DoorLock::LEDSettingEnum;

    static constexpr ClusterId GetClusterId() { return Clusters::DoorLock::Id; }
    static constexpr AttributeId GetAttributeId() { return Attributes::LEDSettings::Id; }
    static constexpr bool MustUseTimedWrite() { return false; }
};
} // namespace LEDSettings
```

