body:
In the copy assignment operator, if `SetLength(other.Length())` fails (when `other.Length() > kCapacity`), the subsequent `memcpy` on line 317 would copy more data than the buffer's capacity, causing buffer overflow. This should check the error: `VerifyOrReturnError(SetLength(other.Length()) == CHIP_NO_ERROR, *this);` to prevent undefined behavior.
```suggestion
        if (SetLength(other.Length()) != CHIP_NO_ERROR)
            return *this;
```

_Originally posted by @bot_01917 in https://github.com/project-chip/connectedhomeip/pull/41866#discussion_r2511713004_

While this change restores the original behavior of always calling `OnCheckInComplete` regardless of storage errors, silently ignoring storage failures could lead to data inconsistency. When `StoreEntry` fails, the updated `clientInfo.offset` won't be persisted, which may cause duplicate check-in messages to be processed in future. Consider adding error logging similar to lines 104, 125, and 132 to make storage failures visible for debugging purposes. For example: `CHIP_ERROR err = mpICDClientStorage->StoreEntry(clientInfo); if (err != CHIP_NO_ERROR) { ChipLogError(ICD, \"Failed to store updated client info: %\" CHIP_ERROR_FORMAT, err.Format()); }`
```suggestion
        CHIP_ERROR storeErr = mpICDClientStorage->StoreEntry(clientInfo);
        if (storeErr != CHIP_NO_ERROR)
        {
            ChipLogError(ICD, "Failed to store updated client info: %" CHIP_ERROR_FORMAT, storeErr.Format());
        }
```

_Originally posted by @bot_01917 in https://github.com/project-chip/connectedhomeip/pull/41923#discussion_r2514515510_

We define our `MeasurementAccuracyStruct` as:
```
struct MeasurementData
{
    Structs::MeasurementAccuracyStruct::Type measurementAccuracy;
    Optional<Structs::EnergyMeasurementStruct::Type> cumulativeImported;
    Optional<Structs::EnergyMeasurementStruct::Type> cumulativeExported;
    Optional<Structs::EnergyMeasurementStruct::Type> periodicImported;
    Optional<Structs::EnergyMeasurementStruct::Type> periodicExported;
    Optional<Structs::CumulativeEnergyResetStruct::Type> cumulativeReset;
};
```

However, we encode Null on the wire when performing a read fore an attribute where the optional doesn't have a value. 

We should address this lack of consistency in the typing.

### Reproduction steps

The following fields (as viewed from .matter) are marked provisional in the spec, but not in the SDK:

```
  # BasicInformation
  provisional readonly attribute int32u configurationVersion = 24;

  # BridgedDeviceBasicInformation
  provisional readonly attribute optional int32u configurationVersion = 24;
```

The following fields (as viewed from .matter) are marked provisional in the SDK, but not in the spec:
```
  # GeneralCommissioning
  readonly attribute access(read: administer) optional int16u TCAcceptedVersion = 5;
  readonly attribute access(read: administer) optional int16u TCMinRequiredVersion = 6;
  readonly attribute access(read: administer) optional bitmap16 TCAcknowledgements = 7;
  readonly attribute access(read: administer) optional boolean TCAcknowledgementsRequired = 8;
  readonly attribute access(read: administer) optional nullable int32u TCUpdateDeadline = 9;

  # NetworkCommissioning
  readonly attribute optional WiFiBandEnum supportedWiFiBands[] = 8;
  readonly attribute optional ThreadCapabilitiesBitmap supportedThreadFeatures = 9;
  readonly attribute optional int16u threadVersion = 10;

  # WakeOnLan
  readonly attribute optional octet_string<16> linkLocalAddress = 1;
```

Incorrect type in SDK vs SPEC:
```
    # SoftwareDiagnostics
    optional octet_string<1024> faultRecording = 2;
```

Also *possibly* non-provisional clusters in the SPEC / data model XML that are still provisional in zap / SDK (needs to be verified):

```
cluster ScenesManagement = 98 {
cluster DeviceEnergyManagement = 152 {
cluster DeviceEnergyManagementMode = 159 {
cluster CommodityPrice
cluster CommodityTariff
cluster CommodityMetering
cluster WebRTCTransportProvider = 1363 {
```

Also, some v1.6 Groupcast work leaked into the v1.5 branch .matter (though cluster Groupcast is correctly marked provisional):

```
  enum AccessControlAuxiliaryTypeEnum : enum8 {
    kSystem = 0;
    kGroupcast = 1;
  }

optional fabric_sensitive AccessControlAuxiliaryTypeEnum auxiliaryType = 5;
```


