### Reproduction steps

In `GenericThreadStackManagerImpl_OpenThread.hpp`, in the `_OnPlatformEvent` method, it seems we generate a `kLinkDown` fault when thread state changed to not attached but we don't delete that fault when link is up/connected.  Right now we only log a message but don't remove the `kLinkDown` on a new event that says everything is good. 

The relevant code is
```
                if (mIsAttached)
                {
                    delegate->OnConnectionStatusChanged(app::Clusters::ThreadNetworkDiagnostics::ConnectionStatusEnum::kConnected);
                }
                else
                {
                    delegate->OnConnectionStatusChanged(
                        app::Clusters::ThreadNetworkDiagnostics::ConnectionStatusEnum::kNotConnected);

                    GeneralFaults<kMaxNetworkFaults> current;
                    current.add(to_underlying(chip::app::Clusters::ThreadNetworkDiagnostics::NetworkFaultEnum::kLinkDown));
                    delegate->OnNetworkFaultChanged(mNetworkFaults, current);
