[2026-03-23T22:27:09Z] user_00168: I keep running into this and I think this might be caused by defunct sessions.

Basically we seem to evict only `if session->IsActiveSession() && session->GetTCPConnection() == conn`. 

If session was already `kDefunct`, it will be skipped, leaving a stale TCP reference (`mTCPConnection`) and keeping `ActiveTCPConnectionState` refcount non-zero (`in-use: false, ref count: 1`), which logs as leaked `UNDEFINED`.

I'll leave the following patch running on my same setup, but here's what I think might be the solution:

```diff
diff --git a/src/transport/SessionManager.cpp b/src/transport/SessionManager.cpp
index 5e191175b0..aedd641cc7 100644
--- a/src/transport/SessionManager.cpp
+++ b/src/transport/SessionManager.cpp
@@ -1328,16 +1328,21 @@ void SessionManager::MarkSecureSessionOverTCPForEviction(Transport::ActiveTCPCon
 {
     // Mark the corresponding secure sessions for eviction
     mSecureSessions.ForEachSession([&](auto session) {
-        if (session->IsActiveSession() && session->GetTCPConnection() == conn)
+        if (session->GetTCPConnection() == conn)
         {
             SessionHandle handle(*session);
             // Notify the SessionConnection delegate of the connection
             // closure.
-            if (mConnDelegate != nullptr)
+            if (session->IsActiveSession() && mConnDelegate != nullptr)
             {
                 mConnDelegate->OnTCPConnectionClosed(conn, handle, conErr);
             }

+            // Always detach the closed TCP connection from the session. Defunct
+            // sessions can still hold a TCP connection reference and otherwise
+            // leak the ActiveTCPConnectionState entry.
+            session->ReleaseTCPConnection();
+
             // Mark session for eviction.
             session->MarkForEviction();
         }
```

cc: @user_00012 @user_00551 

