[2026-04-06T21:34:19Z] user_01132: ### Analysis
The Groupcast cluster commands that modify auxiliary ACL state (JoinGroup, ConfigureAuxiliaryACL, RemoveGroup) all follow the same pattern in GroupcastCluster.cpp — they only emit an event, never an attribute notification.
JoinGroup (lines 492–495):
```
if (groups.ConsumeAuxAclNotificationNeeded())
{
    EmitAuxiliaryAccessUpdated(subjectDescriptor);
}
```
ConfigureAuxiliaryACL (lines 569–572):
```
if (groups.ConsumeAuxAclNotificationNeeded())
{
    EmitAuxiliaryAccessUpdated(subjectDescriptor);
}
```
RemoveGroup (lines 675–678):
```
if (groups.ConsumeAuxAclNotificationNeeded())
{
    EmitAuxiliaryAccessUpdated(subjectDescriptor);
}
```
EmitAuxiliaryAccessUpdated (lines 775–791) only generates the AuxiliaryAccessUpdated event - no attribute notification:
```
void GroupcastCluster::EmitAuxiliaryAccessUpdated(
    const chip::Access::SubjectDescriptor & subjectDescriptor)
{
    AccessControl::Events::AuxiliaryAccessUpdated::Type event;
    event.fabricIndex = subjectDescriptor.fabricIndex;
    // ...
    (void) mContext->interactionContext.eventsGenerator.GenerateEvent(event, kRootEndpointId);
}
```
Meanwhile, the AccessControl cluster at access-control-cluster.cpp has an established pattern for notifying attribute changes on derived lists:
```
void AccessControlCluster::MarkCommissioningRestrictionListChanged()
{
    NotifyAttributeChanged(AccessControl::Attributes::CommissioningARL::Id);
}
void AccessControlCluster::MarkRestrictionListChanged(FabricIndex fabricIndex)
{
    NotifyAttributeChanged(AccessControl::Attributes::Arl::Id);
}
```
No equivalent MarkAuxiliaryACLChanged() method exists, and AuxiliaryACL is never passed to NotifyAttributeChanged or MatterReportingAttributeChangeCallback anywhere in the codebase.
Additionally, the WriteAttribute handler for AccessControl does not handle AuxiliaryACL at all - the attribute is derived from Groupcast group state, not directly writable.


