[2026-07-16T00:10:01Z] user_01132: **Proposed fix (pending agreement this is an SDK issue, not a spec issue)**
**Reading of the spec:** the maxLength 32 constraint on TransferFileDesignator is unconditional in the data model XML. Section 5.1.4 ([Effect on Receipt](https://github.com/CHIP-Specifications/connectedhomeip-spec/blob/06c4d55962954546ecf093c221fe1dab57645028/src/service_device_management/DiagnosticLogsCluster.adoc#514-effect-on-receipt)) explicitly lists its status-code exceptions (INVALID_COMMAND for BDX with no designator, INVALID_COMMAND for out-of-range Intent/RequestedProtocol) and has no carve-out that exempts the designator from constraint validation on non-BDX paths. Under the general rule that a present command field violating its constraint yields CONSTRAINT_ERROR, the check should apply regardless of protocol. Also worth noting that the current implementation doesn't consistently follow either interpretation, since it enforces the constraint on the BDX path but not on the ResponsePayload path.

The proposed change is to hoist the length check in DiagnosticLogsCluster::InvokeCommand out of HandleLogRequestForBdx so it runs whenever the field is present, before the protocol branch:


    case RetrieveLogsRequest::Id: {
        RetrieveLogsRequest::DecodableType commandData;
        ReturnErrorOnFailure(commandData.Decode(input_arguments));
        auto intent   = commandData.intent;
        auto protocol = commandData.requestedProtocol;
        if (intent == IntentEnum::kUnknownEnumValue || protocol == TransferProtocolEnum::kUnknownEnumValue)
        {
            return Status::InvalidCommand;
        }

        // The TransferFileDesignator maxLength constraint is unconditional in the
        // data model: validate it whenever the field is present, regardless of the
        // requested protocol.
        if (commandData.transferFileDesignator.HasValue())
        {
            VerifyOrReturnError(commandData.transferFileDesignator.Value().size() <= kMaxFileDesignatorLen,
                                Status::ConstraintError);
        }
        ...
In addition to the above:

- Remove the now redundant length check in HandleLogRequestForBdx (DiagnosticLogsCluster.cpp:125). The BDX-specific missing designator check that returns INVALID_COMMAND (line 123) stays, since that one is spec mandated.
- Add a unit test in src/app/clusters/diagnostic-logs-server/tests/ covering RequestedProtocol=ResponsePayload with a 33-char designator, expecting ConstraintError.
- Remove the RetrieveLogsRequest entry from COMMAND_CONSTRAINT_DENIED_COMMANDS in src/python_testing/support_modules/idm_support.py (added in #73066), so TC-IDM-9.1 covers this as a regression test going forward.

**Alternative resolution:** if the intended behavior is that TransferFileDesignator is ignored entirely (constraint included) when RequestedProtocol != BDX, then this is a spec issue instead. In that case section 5.1.4 should say so explicitly, the same way it spells out its other exceptions, and the deny-list entry in TC-IDM-9.1 becomes permanent with a comment citing that language.

