### Problem
When `CommodityTariff::Instance` is allocated dynamically (via `new` or `std::make_unique`), the internal pointer `mServerTariffAttrsCtx.mTariffProvider` is left uninitialized. 

As soon as network time synchronizes (SNTP/Matter Epoch), an internal update is triggered (`UpdateCurrentAttrs()`). The null-guard fails because the pointer contains garbage memory instead of `nullptr`, leading to an invalid memory dereference and a firmware crash.

---

### Root Cause
In `src/app/clusters/commodity-tariff-server/commodity-tariff-server.h`:
```cpp
struct CurrentTariffAttrsCtx
{
    Delegate * mTariffProvider; // <-- Uninitialized raw pointer
    EndpointId mEndpointId;
};
```
In `UpdateCurrentAttrs()`, the safety check expects `nullptr` when no tariff data exists:
```cpp
if (mServerTariffAttrsCtx.mTariffProvider == nullptr) // <-- Bypassed because of garbage data
{
    return CHIP_ERROR_NOT_FOUND;
}
// Crash: dereferences mTariffProvider pointing to invalid memory
ReturnErrorOnFailure(UpdateDayInformation(now));
```

---

### Upstream Fix (SDK)
Add default member initialization in `commodity-tariff-server.h`:
```diff
--- a/src/app/clusters/commodity-tariff-server/commodity-tariff-server.h
+++ b/src/app/clusters/commodity-tariff-server/commodity-tariff-server.h
-        Delegate * mTariffProvider;
+        Delegate * mTariffProvider = nullptr;
```

---

### Local Workaround
Until patched upstream, instantiate the cluster with **static storage duration** (`static CommodityTariff::Instance ...`). Static objects are placed in the `.bss` section and guaranteed to be zero-initialized at boot, forcing `mTariffProvider == nullptr`.

